  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following is not correct?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ΔG</mi></math> is negative for a spontaneous reaction",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ΔG</mi></math> is positive for a spontaneous reaction",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ΔG</mi></math> is zero for a reversible reaction",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ΔG</mi></math> is positive for a non-spontaneous reaction",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></math> can be expressed as:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math></p><p>where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></math> is the change in free energy</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> is the change in enthalpy</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> is the temperature</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> is the change in entropy.</p><p>Conditions for spontaneous and non spontaneous reactions in terms of free energy change are as follows,</p><p> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mi>ΔG</mi><mo>&gt;0  </mo></math>for non-sponateneous reaction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mi>ΔG</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo> </mo></math>for spontaneous reaction.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mi>ΔG</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> for equilibrium reaction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>ΔG</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>)</mo><mi>ve</mi></math><span style='font-family: sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, \"Trebuchet MS\", \"Apple Color Emoji\", \"Segoe UI Emoji\", \"Segoe UI Symbol\";'> </span><span style='font-family: sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, \"Trebuchet MS\", \"Apple Color Emoji\", \"Segoe UI Emoji\", \"Segoe UI Symbol\";'>for</span><span style='font-family: sans-serif, Arial, Verdana, \"Trebuchet MS\", \"Apple Color Emoji\", \"Segoe UI Emoji\", \"Segoe UI Symbol\";'> non-spontaneous process</span></p><p>Hence option B is the answer.</p>"
